  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Omni Air International obligated $270M in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. Omni Air International won 148 awards this fiscal year, with an average award size of $1.8M. Omni Air International’s obligations fell 36.6% year over year. Omni Air International’s largest market by NAICS is Nonscheduled Chartered Passenger Air Transportation, which accounted for $269M of obligations in FY2026 to date. Omni Air International also recorded obligations in Scheduled Freight Air Transportation of $785K in FY2026 to date. Omni Air International’s historical fiscal-year obligations include $6.1M in FY21, $12.8M in FY22, $21.5M in FY23, $14.2M in FY24, and $426M in FY25. All figures presented are contract obligations unless otherwise noted, and current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Omni Air International’s federal contracting trended over recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "Omni Air International obligated $6.1M in FY21, $12.8M in FY22, $21.5M in FY23, $14.2M in FY24, $426M in FY25, and $270M in FY26 to date. Omni Air International’s obligations fell 36.6% year over year into FY2026 to date relative to the prior comparable period. Omni Air International’s FY2026 to date total is a partial figure for the fiscal year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What does Omni Air International primarily sell to the federal government?",
        "body": "Omni Air International’s primary market is Nonscheduled Chartered Passenger Air Transportation, which accounted for $269M in obligations in FY2026 to date. Omni Air International also recorded obligations in Scheduled Freight Air Transportation of $785K in FY2026 to date. The stated figures are obligations for the fiscal year to date and reflect the contract activity in those NAICS markets."
      }
    ]
  },
